abstract: >-
  Multi-format research package with four parts. (1) A zero-Mathlib Lean 4.35.0 model of
  the package's integer scoring and access-control rules: 36 core declarations plus 4
  Palomar comparator wrappers, built and checked here. 15 are quantified bound and
  monotonicity facts about the package's own definitions; 21 are closed evaluations,
  literal sums or non-vacuity witnesses that certify no data. (2) A 748-run paired
  in-silico simulation study (11-pool FP64 energy accounting, Holm-Bonferroni corrected
  paired tests) comparing a simulated Ring-0 access-control rule with behavioral
  restraints. (3) An AMS-LaTeX white paper. (4) A crosswalk against a 1,900-problem
  open-problem atlas in which no problem is retired. Five companion repositories report
  a further 291 Lean theorems; these are not built or checked in this package. No
  hardware is modelled in Lean, and the work has not been externally peer reviewed.
